# Keep secrets, local state, and heavy/generated dirs out of the build.
#
# NOTE ON PLACEMENT: Docker only auto-reads the .dockerignore at the *root of the
# build context*. This project's build context is the REPO ROOT (the tsc build
# needs ../shared), so to make these patterns take effect during `docker build`,
# either symlink this file to the repo root:
#     ln -sf automation/.dockerignore ../.dockerignore   # run from automation/
# or copy it there. The Dockerfile also COPYs only the exact paths it needs
# (package manifests, tsconfig, src/, shared/) and never `COPY . .`, so no
# secret or local artifact can enter the image even if this file is not applied —
# the patterns below are defense-in-depth plus a faster, smaller build context.
#
# Patterns use **/ so they match whether the context is the repo root or automation/.

# Secrets / credentials — never ship these into an image layer
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.auth-state.json
**/firebase-service-account*.json
**/*serviceAccount*.json
**/serviceAccountKey*.json

# Local runtime output
**/proofs/
**/data/

# Dependencies + build output (rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# VCS / editor / OS cruft
.git/
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*

# Docker + docs (not needed at build time)
**/Dockerfile
**/docker-compose*.yml
**/.dockerignore
**/DEPLOY.md
**/*.md
